# Cases - the mirrored fixtures themselves, one subchapter per test-examples/ dir. This
# directory's OWN .yo/meta.yo types the cases: one pattern clause selects every 4-digit
# member and mounts its fixture files as TEXT (docs/meta/members) - the first meta-typed
# chapter in the book.
Cases
description: the mirrored fixtures - each file shown as the code it is, byte-exact
- >
  Every case below is typed by ONE clause in this directory's `.yo/meta.yo`: a
  `pattern: true` selector matches the 4-digit names, and its nested `members:` mounts
  `in.yo` and `out.yo` as yamlover CODE and `ir.json` as json code - text, not parsed
  subtrees, because a fixture's files are byte goldens
  ([the members clause](*::meta:members)).
- *: '0000'
- *: '0001'
- *: '0002'
- *: '0003'
- *: '0004'
- *: '0005'
- *: '0006'
- *: '0007'
- *: '0008'
- *: '0100'
